# Architecture Plan: Full Data Access Migration (Retire Direct Prisma)

## 0. Executive Summary
**Goal**: Fully eliminate direct `prisma.*` calls from the application layer (API Routes, Actions, Components).
**Pattern**: Specialized Ports & Adapters (Hybrid).
**Outcome**: A modular, testable, and database-agnostic core application.

---

## 1. Domain Analysis & Repository Scope
Based on codebase analysis, we identified 7 distinct domains requiring repositories.

| Domain | Scope | Entities Managed | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Tasks** | Core Task Management | [Task](file:///home/resgef/works/notion-clone/src/types/domain/task.ts#1-14), `TaskAssignee`, `TaskActionLog`, `Subtasks` | 🟡 Partial |
| **Users** | Identity & Auth | `User`, `Account`, `Session` | 🔴 Missing |
| **Boards** | Project Structure | [Board](file:///home/resgef/works/notion-clone/src/repositories/ITaskRepository.ts#4-8), `Column`, `Membership`, `Sprint` | 🔴 Missing |
| **Organizations** | Tenants | `Organization`, `OrganizationMember` | 🔴 Missing |
| **Comments** | Collaboration | `TaskComment` | 🔴 Missing |
| **Time** | Work Logs | `TaskTimeEntry` | 🔴 Missing (Mixed in Task) |
| **Tags** | Metadata | `Tag`, `TaskTag` | 🔴 Missing |

---

## 2. Architecture Visualizations

### A. The Target Architecture
The application layer (API Routes) talks **only** to Interfaces.

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Application Layer"
        API["API Routes / Server Actions"]
    end

    subgraph "Domain Layer (Interfaces)"
        ITask["ITaskRepository"]
        IUser["IUserRepository"]
        IBoard["IBoardRepository"]
    end

    subgraph "Infrastructure Layer (Implementations)"
        PrismaTask["PrismaTaskRepository"]
        PrismaUser["PrismaUserRepository"]
        PrismaBoard["PrismaBoardRepository"]
        PrismaClient[("Prisma Client (Global)")]
    end

    API --> ITask
    API --> IUser
    API --> IBoard

    ITask -.-> PrismaTask
    IUser -.-> PrismaUser
    IBoard -.-> PrismaBoard

    PrismaTask --> PrismaClient
    PrismaUser --> PrismaClient
    PrismaBoard --> PrismaClient

    classDef interface fill:#e1f5fe,stroke:#01579b,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef impl fill:#f3e5f5,stroke:#4a148c,stroke-width:2px;
    class ITask,IUser,IBoard interface;
    class PrismaTask,PrismaUser,PrismaBoard impl;
```

### B. Request Flow (Example: Assign User to Task)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Ctrl as API Route (POST /assign)
    participant Repo as TaskRepository
    participant DB as Prisma Client
    participant Log as Logger (ActionLog)

    Ctrl->>Repo: assignUser(taskId, userId)
    
    rect rgb(240, 240, 255)
        Note right of Repo: Transaction Boundary
        Repo->>DB: create(TaskAssignee)
        Repo->>DB: create(TaskActionLog)
    end
    
    DB-->>Repo: Success
    Repo-->>Ctrl: Updated Task
    Ctrl-->>Client: 200 OK
```

